{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2","id":"pg_848b24ea291a53c79a4b771c2b2946be","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhnt-loushang-docs-internals-architecture-coding-component-interfaces--771c2b2946be.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ad848a6b174a54a5ab75e875adad1e4c"],"title":"zhnt/loushang/docs/internals/architecture/coding/component-interfaces/tools.md @ 89d885f53c1a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2","id":"pg_979eaada50dd5c4c918f8950173af18a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhnt-loushang-docs-internals-architecture-coding-component-interfaces--8950173af18a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_0d09b40e4e985af2a789f42818f64122"],"title":"zhnt/loushang/docs/internals/architecture/coding/component-interfaces/workflow.md @ 89d885f53c1a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_36850e209d5ad562c9fe5522e7deaea9b40cf63a15c48000e5c727f292e347ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent loop remains owned by loushang.agent; plugins may contribute tools, resources, capability providers, and adapters but cannot replace its state machine."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3bca7e114ba718fa0234897b938aadf034bdf90c90018b1de224e77f933eec5d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin runtime manifest is a strict plugin.json carrying identity, version, engine range, contribution index, configuration schema, dependencies, requested authority, and execution topology."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57338955f7519da31ab6a1dcd5465cb40648e912aefd623b7fa5beed8ccc6c63"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Plugin discovery, inspection, dependency solving, and selection operate on inert serializable data and never import modules or run scripts; execution starts only after revalidation of revision, scope, authority, and approval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5d164e60f352336836b10738691eba4c0ee9e4baa87d510a87a9a5665f00db23"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The current PyPI materializer can invoke uv pip install/pip install without wheel-only or contained build service, which the document calls an explicit current security gap for untrusted plugin admission."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6f20407cb0f47be747b4458f6e55972ef3308f67b300aaa3bd564eede04c21d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The threat model assumes plugins and dependencies may be malicious or compromised, and mandates fail-closed handling of traversal, symlink escape, approval replay, stale IPC, and output floods."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7e2d1c9d73000aa14376b7b18de478a16a07b0660ca1443fbd71c2d37e4f7530"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin architecture document states implementation is partial: strict codecs, ledgers, and some coding paths exist, while the public SDK, managed Skill actions, and isolated Plugin Workers remain future delivery work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c3d4b2a534ce839726525a6c572f1d41238c45bcc6a2a19fec109f3b76197c02"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Manifests may request authority but cannot grant it, self-mark trust, choose sandbox exemptions, or widen product policy; trust is evaluated by Host-owned policy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cb197ff0b99e1c364b2a8cf847282e21d897324035c16dd0492420229308cf7f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills are typed Resource projections containing instructions, metadata, assets, and optional scripts; script existence grants no execution authority, and the catalog/Skill parser never executes scripts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d4ea3da642146da12e478885cc91159d3e75f10232bd0e13e8eca10027f2060d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Process isolation is treated as distinct from security isolation: Policy, Approval, Sandbox, Host, and Domain are separate axes, and required containment fails closed before spawn."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d80b16e83656ad4a5d617dafcf0a548c425635363c621e570fb4dce15ac9c91d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture keeps declaration axes independent (artifact, identity, contribution, capability, execution topology, trust, lifetime, scope), so resource/capability/worker/remote are not Plugin types."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f57466bc7d9cd4e5ff7b201c2023c3995ad5eab8888f97437363b9fbf064a200"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The accepted plugin architecture treats a Plugin as an independently selectable activation identity grouping typed contributions, distinct from Capability, Skill, Tool, Extension, or process."}],"claim_ids":["clm_36850e209d5ad562c9fe5522e7deaea9b40cf63a15c48000e5c727f292e347ec","clm_3bca7e114ba718fa0234897b938aadf034bdf90c90018b1de224e77f933eec5d","clm_57338955f7519da31ab6a1dcd5465cb40648e912aefd623b7fa5beed8ccc6c63","clm_5d164e60f352336836b10738691eba4c0ee9e4baa87d510a87a9a5665f00db23","clm_6f20407cb0f47be747b4458f6e55972ef3308f67b300aaa3bd564eede04c21d6","clm_7e2d1c9d73000aa14376b7b18de478a16a07b0660ca1443fbd71c2d37e4f7530","clm_c3d4b2a534ce839726525a6c572f1d41238c45bcc6a2a19fec109f3b76197c02","clm_cb197ff0b99e1c364b2a8cf847282e21d897324035c16dd0492420229308cf7f","clm_d4ea3da642146da12e478885cc91159d3e75f10232bd0e13e8eca10027f2060d","clm_d80b16e83656ad4a5d617dafcf0a548c425635363c621e570fb4dce15ac9c91d","clm_f57466bc7d9cd4e5ff7b201c2023c3995ad5eab8888f97437363b9fbf064a200"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2","id":"pg_d8fb185614d25c72b98dfbf32ecd64ea","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhnt-loushang-docs-internals-architecture-harness-plugin-architecture--fbf32ecd64ea.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9d2505e27d7550328ad9a442fa3f4e45"],"title":"zhnt/loushang/docs/internals/architecture/harness/plugin/architecture.md @ 89d885f53c1a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0fc68fde52d563550c27d6e11d9e914f76e1dd35ea55c1d3430629e4f85c4526"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions are durable coding conversations that can be resumed, forked, exported, and inspected, with diagnostics available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_398429fd77078216e050041812640bbc8965511e7f55d0e0f3d041d4f761a2d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Loushang is described as a method-native AI work system for running complex work from intent to verified delivery, with the current focus on a coding CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3b80c839ff4fe94da270af5359e37313e09a844637af63371223825f0f54a925"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system is organized into named layers: method (work contract), work (runtime fact), agent (execution kernel), ai (model access), harness (substrate), coding (V1 surface), tui, and channel."},{"claim_ids":["clm_42db6cd5c884fa23bd3ce3a04528b19747e16c2ce8ef2b2e014b0f81a33ee28d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools are defined as executable capabilities made available to the agent under policy, and the product offers built-in coding tools plus configurable tool surfaces."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a5d20332662bed4cd17db01f11749498d0cee804c323974803fdfeaf0e9285be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes flags such as --help, --list-models, and --list-commands, and supports a prompt mode like `loushang -p \"...\"` for one-shot requests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ce0c26e1443a55dcd3d480879215783cda2d0eb8cd3edf9da5c64f2c5156e9f6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Loushang is in active early development; the stable focus is loushang code and the loushang.ai SDK, while work/research/ppt surfaces are roadmap directions only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d428b6c2a8c8ab8f42e7ca5cd2982410a2a09c712538d9823e70ecdbb1098b01"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The loushang.ai SDK appears to provide provider-aware model access with a model registry, streaming, tool calls, and cost helpers, per the README feature list."},{"claim_ids":["clm_db479b2adfa4034bcbfe216baf5a4cb738155f64a63a478793da4855d3dbea29"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project uses uv for virtual environment creation and pip-style editable installation with a [dev] extra, and third-party dependency information is documented in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f6aa6fda4581943d3b9bece0fa2d52aa2b67e2bcf99086b34e0482a972f63d90"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the recommended way to run Loushang is from source via git clone, a uv-created .venv, and editable install with the dev extra; `make bootstrap` automates this and no `make install` target exists."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0fc68fde52d563550c27d6e11d9e914f76e1dd35ea55c1d3430629e4f85c4526","clm_398429fd77078216e050041812640bbc8965511e7f55d0e0f3d041d4f761a2d5","clm_3b80c839ff4fe94da270af5359e37313e09a844637af63371223825f0f54a925","clm_42db6cd5c884fa23bd3ce3a04528b19747e16c2ce8ef2b2e014b0f81a33ee28d","clm_a5d20332662bed4cd17db01f11749498d0cee804c323974803fdfeaf0e9285be","clm_ce0c26e1443a55dcd3d480879215783cda2d0eb8cd3edf9da5c64f2c5156e9f6","clm_d428b6c2a8c8ab8f42e7ca5cd2982410a2a09c712538d9823e70ecdbb1098b01","clm_db479b2adfa4034bcbfe216baf5a4cb738155f64a63a478793da4855d3dbea29","clm_f6aa6fda4581943d3b9bece0fa2d52aa2b67e2bcf99086b34e0482a972f63d90"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2","id":"pg_fe594e74fe0350ad8c88a768d3911c92","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhnt-loushang-readme-md-89d885f53c1a-a768d3911c92.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c6614789a2475064b7aab9c950e7a14c"],"title":"zhnt/loushang/README.md @ 89d885f53c1a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:27:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_440a939d464c4469953f2da01ff19bb2"}
